  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improve citizen participation in decentralized governance process</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The CEJP will conduct an identification of different laws in relation to human rights, to principles of good governance, to important policies of the country such as decentralization.   Knowledge of laws encourage citizen&apos;s address to the authorities to claim his rights expression. Understanding the operation of the decentralized administration (local authorities and their responsibilities, mandates, etc) will allow people to easily obtain services and be able to claim from the senior ranks. The project will also inform the population about the current programs and the importance of their involvement and will allow the population to participate in the &apos;open door - day&apos; organised by the local administration (district and sector) each quarter.</narrative>
  </description>
